From 732b4140d791781ea17d38575e9c47667c468b0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:34:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): reject unresolvable worktree workspaces at
 create; block on first spawn [daveey]

kanban_create / hermes kanban create now validate a non-project worktree
workspace with the resolver's own rules (linked worktree, repo root, or a
path whose parent is in a repo; no path -> board default_workdir) and return
an error naming the fix (worktree:<repo root>, or git -C <repo> worktree add
...), suggesting the sibling repo for <repo>-<slug> names.

The resolver raises WorktreeWorkspaceConfigError for these deterministic
cases; the dispatcher force-trips it (sticky) on the first spawn failure
instead of burning the retry budget. Transient workspace errors still retry.
---
